From 7c627dc90567741d0771f47b1c425f33e6674748 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 11:11:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add the Jacobi preconditioner by nodal blocks

NodalBlockJacobi inverts, node by node, the blocks of the matrix which
couple the components of the unknown at each node (3 x 3 blocks in three
dimensional mechanics), with the batched dense linear algebra of MFEM:
native kernels, cuBLAS or hipBLAS, or MAGMA (option Backend, the active
backend of MFEM by default), the inverses being applied by batched
products or the LU factors by batched solves (option Factorization). The
blocks are extracted by a kernel from the sparse matrix, or from the
diagonal block of each process of the matrix of hypre, read where hypre
stores it. The unknowns may be ordered by nodes, the vectors being then
gathered and scattered, or by vector dimension.

The backends cuBLAS, hipBLAS and MAGMA compute on their own queue: the
device is synchronized around their operations. Without it, with MAGMA,
the GMRES solver of MFEM in parallel on the GPU gave to MAGMA vectors
still being computed, and diverged.
